From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:25:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] core/compositor: don't seed a subsurface's extends() at
 the toplevel origin

breadthfirst() reports every subsurface at its offset relative to the
toplevel surface, including the root when the root is itself a
subsurface. extends() also seeded the region with {0, 0, size}, so a
subsurface's extents covered both its real box and a phantom box at the
toplevel's origin.

A subsurface placed under a header bar therefore compared equal to its
parent's extents. getSolitaryResource() and findWithCM() then treated it
as covering the whole window. GTK 4 graphics offload hits this: WebKitGTK
puts the web view in an opaque XR24 subsurface at (0, 46) below the main
surface, and the window was judged opaque.
---
 src/protocols/core/Compositor.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/protocols/core/Compositor.cpp b/src/protocols/core/Compositor.cpp
index ddc034d2..c5e4bfad 100644
--- a/src/protocols/core/Compositor.cpp
+++ b/src/protocols/core/Compositor.cpp
@@ -553,7 +553,13 @@ SP<CWlSurface> CWLSurfaceResource::getResource() {
 }
 
 CBox CWLSurfaceResource::extends() {
-    CRegion full = CBox{{}, m_current.size};
+    // breadthfirst() hands every subsurface its offset relative to the toplevel surface, and that
+    // includes this surface when it is itself a subsurface. Seeding the region with {0,0,size} as
+    // well would add a phantom box at the toplevel's origin, so a subsurface placed below a header
+    // bar would appear to cover the whole window. Only a non-subsurface root starts at the origin.
+    CRegion full;
+    if (!m_role || m_role->role() != SURFACE_ROLE_SUBSURFACE)
+        full = CBox{{}, m_current.size};
     breadthfirst(
         [](SP<CWLSurfaceResource> surf, const Vector2D& offset, void* d) {
             if (surf->m_role->role() != SURFACE_ROLE_SUBSURFACE)
